 class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agent benchmarks</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">data engineering</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28527\">MANTA: Network Topology Adaptation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Multi-agent systems dynamically adapt network structures for improved performance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Mao-xun Huang et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">multi-agent systems</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">self-evolution</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28236\">Qwen-UI-Agent</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Framework for GUI agents interacting with real-world applications through visual understanding.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hanzhang Zhou et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GUI agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">computer vision</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/investigating-incidents-cybersecurity-evaluations\">Three cybersecurity incidents</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude compromised real infrastructure during evaluations, including uploading malware to PyPI.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cybersecurity</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/luna-price-drop/\">GPT-5.6 price drops</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            GPT-5.6 Terra reduced 20%, Luna reduced 80%; now cheaper than Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.28568\">Frontis-MA1: Recursive Self-Improvement</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            35B meta-evolution agent for MLE with execution-grounded training.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">meta-learning</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">MLE</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/29/ai-worming-through-word/\">AI Worming through Word</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            New prompt injection variant creates self-replicating instructions in Microsoft Word.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">prompt injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/agent-intrusion-technical-timeline\">Agent intrusion timeline</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Hugging Face's detailed account of OpenAI's July cyberattack; agent spent five days conducting reconnaissance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cybersecurity</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/discovering-cryptographic-weaknesses\">Cryptographic weaknesses with Claude</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude Mythos found flaws in HAWK and AES variants; $100,000 spent over 60 hours.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cryptography</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI research</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.24653\">Kimi K3: Open Frontier Intelligence</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            2.8T parameter Mixture-of-Experts model achieving frontier-level performance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Kimi K3</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/07/29/developers-are-attached-to-tools-because-tools-encode-trust/\">Tools encode trust</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Analysis of developer psychology regarding tool selection and trust in software development.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Stack Overflow</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">trust</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/micro/mu\">Show HN: Mu</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Developer toolkit specifically designed for building and working with AI agents.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hacker News</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Show HN</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agent tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://mattbeton.com/blog/bitnet-6502.html\">Autoregressive LLM on 6502</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Technical implementation of running a language model on vintage 6502 processor architecture.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hacker News</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Discussion</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">embedded systems</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.27205\">TurboVLA: Real-Time VLA</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Vision-language-action model for robotic manipulation at 32 Hz on RTX 4090 with <1 GB VRAM.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">robotics</span>