cts (12)</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/w4n9H/autocoder-nano\">autocoder-nano</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Lightweight CLI-based AI coding agent with code generation, AI chat, agent mode, file management, code indexing with RAG, rule engine, and git integration.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 9</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/hotovo/aider-desk\">aider-desk</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Platform for AI-powered software engineers. Electron-based application providing workspace for AI-assisted development work.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI desktop app</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 7</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/milanglacier/minuet-ai.el\">Minuet AI</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Emacs package providing code completion from popular LLMs including OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, Ollama, Llama.cpp, and Codestral.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">IDE integration</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 13</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/jamsocket/forevervm\">ForeverVM</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Secure sandbox environment for executing AI-generated code with persistent state between sessions.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow tool</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 18</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/Illuvien/illuvien\">Illuvien</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Drag-and-drop AI agent builder for visually constructing LLM workflows and deploying as APIs with one click.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow tool</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 11</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/MatterAIOrg/matter-ai\">Matter AI</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Open-source AI code reviewer agent that analyzes pull requests with PR summaries, code review comments, and security vulnerability detection.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI code reviewer</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 10</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/SamYuan1990/OpenAI_CodeAgent-action\">OpenAI CodeAgent-action</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            GitHub Action using OpenAI API for CI/ workflows with AST analysis for unit test generation, docs, and CVE scanning.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow automation</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 10</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/davidorex/project-handoffs\">project-handoffs</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            MCP server for maintaining persistence across AI coding agent sessions with workflow chain and task history tracking.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow tool</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 10</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/AI-Voodoo/BugOut\">BugOut</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Local Pythonic coding agent using DeepSeek Lite API with streaming responses and iterative refinement.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding agent</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 12</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/qudeai/qudeai-framework-v.1\">QudeAI Framework</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            CLI framework for creating AI agents in terminal with Solana blockchain deployment and natural language interaction.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 11</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/thisguypranav/ai_agents\">ai_agents</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Terminal task agent CLI for developers powered by NLP & AI for organizing and managing tasks.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 11</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/maheshbansod/ai.nvim\">ai.nvim</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Neovim plugin with AI functionality including quick change mode and chat interface with Google Gemini API.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">IDE integration</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jan 8</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <div class=\"column\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">Product Updates (8)</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Cursor: Google Workspace Plugins</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Coding agents now have direct access to Gmail, Google Drive, Calendar, Docs, Sheets, and Google Chat.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Aug 3</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Cursor for iPad Released</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            AI-powered coding expanded to tablet devices with inbox feature and full PR review experience.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 29</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\">Codex CLI v0.146.0</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Session management with /new and /clear commands, thread pinning, Agent Plugins support, WebSocket connections, improved Windows compatibility.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 29</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Cursor Start Feature Launch</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            New ₹649 monthly plan for developers in India with local pricing and UPI payment options.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\">Gemini CLI v0.53.0</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            LLM triage orchestrator, container build setup, evaluation coverage reports, workspace trust enforcement, and security fixes.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/features/copilot\">GitHub Copilot Data Training Policy</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Now uses interactions from Copilot subscribers to train AI models unless users opt out.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Policy</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 24</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Cursor Router Released</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Intelligent model router with three optimization modes: Intelligence, Balance, and Cost.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 22</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\">Codex CLI v0.145.0</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Paginated history, /import for migrating settings, Amazon Bedrock support, audio inputs, stabilized multi-agent V2.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 21</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <div class=\"column\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights (20)</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/2/open-letters/\">Open letters about AI development</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Microsoft's open weights letter vs Anthropic's counter-argument; 1,324 AI employees request international governance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI policy</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">governance</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/1/ten-advances-in-mathematics/\">Ten advances in mathematics</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            OpenAI's Astra model solved ten mathematical problems unsolved for over a decade.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">mathematics</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/31/stateless-mcp/\">Stateless MCP</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            MCP 2.0 specification release with new tools: mcp-explorer and datasette-mcp.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">MCP 2.0</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer tools</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/31/deepseek-v4-flash-0731/\">DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            304B parameter model with excellent intelligence-to-cost ratio; improves with high reasoning effort.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">DeepSeek</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28033\">DataClawEval Benchmark</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Evaluation framework for data engineering agents in real industrial environments.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Debin Meng et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agent benchmarks</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">data engineering</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28527\">MANTA: Network Topology Adaptation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Multi-agent systems dynamically adapt network structures for improved performance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Mao-xun Huang et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">multi-agent systems</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">self-evolution</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28236\">Qwen-UI-Agent</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Framework for GUI agents interacting with real-world applications through visual understanding.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hanzhang Zhou et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GUI agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">computer vision</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/investigating-incidents-cybersecurity-evaluations\">Three cybersecurity incidents</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude compromised real infrastructure during evaluations, including uploading malware to PyPI.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cybersecurity</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/luna-price-drop/\">GPT-5.6 price drops</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            GPT-5.6 Terra reduced 20%, Luna reduced 80%; now cheaper than Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.28568\">Frontis-MA1: Recursive Self-Improvement</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            35B meta-evolution agent for MLE with execution-grounded training.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">meta-learning</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">MLE</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/29/ai-worming-through-word/\">AI Worming through Word</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            New prompt injection variant creates self-replicating instructions in Microsoft Word.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">prompt injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/agent-intrusion-technical-timeline\">Agent intrusion timeline</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Hugging Face's detailed account of OpenAI's July cyberattack; agent spent five days conducting reconnaissance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cybersecurity</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/discovering-cryptographic-weaknesses\">Cryptographic weaknesses with Claude</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude Mythos found flaws in HAWK and AES variants; $100,000 spent over 60 hours.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Simon Willison</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">cryptography</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI research</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.24653\">Kimi K3: Open Frontier Intelligence</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            2.8T parameter Mixture-of-Experts model achieving frontier-level performance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Kimi K3</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/07/29/developers-are-attached-to-tools-because-tools-encode-trust/\">Tools encode trust</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Analysis of developer psychology regarding tool selection and trust in software development.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Stack Overflow</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">trust</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/micro/mu\">Show HN: Mu</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Developer toolkit specifically designed for building and working with AI agents.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hacker News</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Show HN</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agent tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://mattbeton.com/blog/bitnet-6502.html\">Autoregressive LLM on 6502</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Technical implementation of running a language model on vintage 6502 processor architecture.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hacker News</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Discussion</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">embedded systems</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.27205\">TurboVLA: Real-Time VLA</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Vision-language-action model for robotic manipulation at 32 Hz on RTX 4090 with <1 GB VRAM.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">robotics</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">real-time AI</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2607.27380\">VideoCoCo: Code-as-CoT</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Framework where executable Blender code serves as chain-of-thought for video generation.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Hugging Face</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">Paper</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">video generation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">code generation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28048\">SKILL-KD: Skill Distillation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Distilling specialized capabilities from LLMs into agent systems using contrastive learning.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"author-name\">Qiming Shi et al.</span> | <span class=\"source-badge\">ArXiv</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">skill distillation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </m